## 4. Conditions (the control ladder)

All conditions share: identical frozen fact stream (replay bypasses buffer dedup — §7), consolidation forced at session end for every session (surprise gate disabled via threshold 1.1; surprise still *computed and logged* for C1 and decorrelation checks), `facts.max_total: 8`, **`facts.admission_gate: true`** (§8 step 3 — at capacity, incoming fact admitted only if its priority exceeds the min-priority victim's; else rejected and logged), **`sleep.prune_on_graduation: false`** and eviction over all non-pruned entries by pure priority (graduation neither frees slots nor grants eviction immunity → capacity is exactly 8 for every condition), `lora.uniform_reps: true` (reps = 2 constant), `lora.augment_paraphrases: 0`, identical sleep schedule, `memit.enabled: false`, `micro_sleep.enabled: false`.

| ID | Name | Selector | LLM call? | Self-model? | Provenance in prompt? | Rescore + self-update? |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| C0 | **RANDOM** | `random.Random(seed).uniform(0,1)` per fact | no | no | no | no |
| C1 | **SURPRISE** (current system) | Per-consolidation-moment SurpriseEstimator score, recomputed offline by calling `evaluate(user_text, new_facts, len(new_facts))` **exactly as chat.py:250 does** (per-turn survivor lists and user text recorded in the freeze) — bit-identical reproduction including the novelty-degeneracy quirk (realized priority = 0.625 + 0.375·marker; see §2 scope 6) | no | no | no | no |
| C2 | **BORROWED** (static regex rules) | Keyword/regex rule table `experiments/data/borrowed_rules.yaml` (health/safety 1.0, user-identity 0.9, schedule/commitments 0.8, preferences 0.5, third-party trivia 0.2, decor/ambient 0.1, default 0.4). Committed **before the corpus exists**; never updated (deliberately blind to the goal shift) | no | no | no | no |
| C3 | **JUDGE** (generic LLM + generic counterfactual) | One batched call per consolidation moment. Context block = **neutral filler text token-matched to the charter**. Instruction (common counterfactual structure, no self/user/charter reference): *"For each fact: if this fact were permanently forgotten, how much future harm would result? 0–10."* Same template, listing format, greedy decoding, parser, and fallback as C4 | yes (1/moment) | no | no | no |
| C3b | **JUDGE-RULES** (borrowed criterion via LLM) | Same call as C3 but the filler is replaced by the **committed borrowed_rules text rendered as prose, token-matched to the charter**; same generic counterfactual instruction as C3. Separates "any explicit criterion helps" from "self-model-referenced criterion helps" (P2b) | yes (1/moment) | no (borrowed rules) | no | no |
