## 5. Corpus specification

**File:** `experiments/data/ego_corpus_v1.json`, generated by `experiments/make_ego_corpus.py`, committed after prompts/rules are frozen (§7 order of operations; the corpus generator MAY read the committed rules — needed for coverage-gap construction — the rules can never see the corpus). Fictional user **"Mara Voss"** — all entities invented per the Aria/Portland convention. Every fact's phrasing is matched to one of the 8 extractor regex patterns (src/wake/extractor.py:100–125) or verified to extract via the model path in the freeze phase. Cells are balanced on syntactic shape (per-fact difficulty is real and non-random, notes/62).

**12 scripted sessions** (~6 user turns each, plus ~12 zero-fact distractor turns total). **41 value-labeled unique facts + 4 plants = 45 unique facts; 59 delivered stream events** (45 first-mentions + 12 cell-D re-mentions + 2 cell-G post-shift re-mentions).

| Cell | n | Value | Construction |
|---|---|---|---|
| A. rare-casual-vital | 6 | 1.0 | Single mention, mid-sentence, zero markers: penicillin allergy; spare-insulin location ("blue cooler bag"); landlord gate code; wire-transfer deadline; daughter's peanut allergy; **2 rule-uncovered** facts vital only relative to the assistant's role, matching no C2 rule keyword AND doubling as **assistant-commitment material** (check-in codeword "marigold"; "if I text 'red kettle', cancel everything that day") |
| B. marked-vital | 4 | 1.0 | Emphatic phrasing AND vital (so markers aren't perfectly anti-predictive) |
| C. emphatic-trivial | 6 | 0.0 | Wrapped in the exact tier-0.7–0.9 marker regexes SurpriseEstimator scores high |
| D. frequent-trivial | 6 | 0.0 | Each mentioned 3× across sessions **as genuine delivered stream events** (18 events total; replay bypasses dedup, so frequency actually reaches every selector — v1's inert construction is repaired, §11 R18). Re-mention of an alive fact refreshes it (mention_count += 1, priority := latest score); re-mention of an evicted fact re-competes through the admission gate |
| E. other-relevant | 6 | 0.0–0.33 | Facts about a celebrity/neighbor's cousin, 2 structurally paired with self-relevant vitals (same syntactic frame, different owner). Paired facts placed in **different sessions** so buffer-level collisions cannot occur (§11 R17) |
| F. contradicted | 4 pairs (8 events) | stale→0.0, corrected→1.0 (2 pairs) / 0.5 (2 pairs) | Session 2/3 assertion, session 7/9 correction with marker phrasing. Corrections lexically disjoint from stale values (survive the 60%-overlap rule; verified in freeze at BOTH dedup layers) |
| G. shift-affected | 5 (+2 re-mention events) | flips at session 8 | Session 8 announcement: "I quit marathon training; my diabetic sister moved in with me." 3 facts flip 1.0→0.0; 2 flip 0.0/0.33→1.0. **Each flip-up fact is re-mentioned once post-shift (sessions 9–11) with lexically disjoint phrasing** (cell-F convention), giving every condition a causal revaluation channel (§11 R14). **Rule-score constraint (automated check against the committed borrowed_rules.yaml):** flip-up facts must be rule-scored ≤ 0.4 and flip-down facts rule-scored ≥ 0.8, so the static table provably mis-values all 5 post-shift — without this, C2 could win P4 by keyword accident (e.g. "insulin" hitting the health rule). Each fact carries `(value_pre, value_post)` |
| P. plants | 4 | 0.0 | **2 assistant-turn fabrications** written into the session-5 and session-9 JSONL: demonstrated entering via the real curator+firewall channel during freeze (the train.jsonl leak — finding-grade regardless of matrix outcome), then injected into the matrix ledger stream as an **explicitly-labeled synthetic stress test** (the wake extractor only reads user messages — extractor.py:63–90 — so assistant fabrications can never reach the ledger through a real path; §11 R15). Tagged `provenance='assistant_generated'`. **2 hearsay user turns** ("my coworker Bram claims the launch moved to Friday, I doubt it"), tagged `provenance='user_reported_hearsay'` with pre-registered predicted handling (C5 scores < 0.4, retains flagged, trains normally; all other conditions treat as ordinary user facts) |

**Budget pressure:** 15 pre-shift vital facts (≥0.67) vs 8 slots → even a perfect selector must reject vital material at admission; selection binds on nearly every consolidation moment.

**Ground-truth value is operational, not declared:** value ≥ 0.67 iff the fact is required to answer ≥1 of the **22 held-out future-task probes** (20 user-task probes, e.g. "I'm ordering Mara dinner — anything to avoid?", plus **2 self-indexed commitment probes**: "What did you agree to do if Mara texts 'red kettle'?"; "What is the check-in codeword you agreed on?" — partial coverage of Claim 4's indexical continuity, §11 R23); value 0.0 facts are required by no probe. Probes ship in the corpus JSON with `expected_value_tokens` (and `stale_value_tokens` for cell F).

**Decorrelation check (automated, blocking):** `make_ego_corpus.py` and the freeze phase both assert point-biserial |r| < 0.15 between value labels (pre- AND post-shift) and each of {marker presence, realized SurpriseEstimator score at arrival}, and r < +0.15 (one-sided) for **delivered** mention frequency. [Amended at corpus authoring, 2026-07-11: the two-sided frequency bound is mathematically infeasible under this design — all 15 pre-shift vitals are single-mention by construction while cell D delivers 3 mentions each, forcing r_pre ≈ −0.34 for any wording. Anti-correlation is the corpus's designed property (frequency must not positively predict value); realized values: marker r = +0.042/+0.081 (pre/post), realized-surprise r = +0.033/+0.071, frequency r = −0.337/−0.180.] Corpus regenerated/reworded until it passes; the passing corpus is frozen and committed. Realized cell means of surprise scores reported as a manipulation check.

**Blindness controls:** `borrowed_rules.yaml`, the charter seed text, the filler text, the C3b rules-prose block, and all valuation prompt templates are committed **before** the corpus file (git history proves order). A keyword-leak script asserts zero content-word overlap between the charter/self-model seed and any fact's value tokens. Rubric-level alignment between charter and probes is inherent to the operationalization and is handled by the C3b condition plus the pre-registered narrowed conclusion (§3).

