## 6. Metrics definitions

**Determinism statement (corrected from v1):** selection-level metrics are deterministic *conditional on the logged valuation outputs and realized graduation events*. Valuation calls after sleep 1 run on fused weights, so LoRA seed variation propagates into C3/C3b/C4/C5 scores (inherent; fully logged). With `prune_on_graduation: false` and pure-priority eviction, graduation no longer perturbs ledger capacity or eviction order, but graduation outcomes themselves remain stochastic (temp-0.3 generation) and are reported, not assumed.

**Primary — selection level:**
- **M1. Value-weighted retention (VWR):** Σ value over **retained** facts ÷ value of the **best achievable retained set**. `retained := (not pruned) OR graduated` — computed from full ledger JSON snapshots (never via `get_active_qa_pairs()`; graduated-implies-pruned was a v1 incoherence, repaired by `prune_on_graduation: false` in the matrix, §11 R16). Denominator = the value of the optimal admission/eviction policy **simulated offline on the frozen event sequence under the actual mechanics** (capacity 8, admission gate, arrival order, re-mention semantics; graduation excluded from the simulation and reported as a guardrail) — not the abstract best-8 set, which is causally unachievable. Snapshotted after every consolidation and every sleep. Pre-shift labels before session 8, post-shift labels after.
- **M2. Ledger composition:** critical-fact survival; **slot waste** (slots holding value-0 facts); per-cell breakdown — **cell-A survival is the single most diagnostic number** (predicted C1 ≈ C0; C4/C5 high); rule-uncovered-subset survival (C2/C3b vs C4). Guardrails: slot-occupancy, cumulative-graduation trajectory, and admission-rejection log per condition (so capacity/churn divergence is visible, not silent).
- **M3. Selection quality ρ:** Spearman(assigned priority, value label) over all scored facts, per consolidation moment. The global-null disambiguator (if ρ separates conditions but recall doesn't, the consolidation stage — not the selector — is the bottleneck: itself a publishable finding about where an ego can matter at 3B).
- **M4. Cycles-to-revalue** (post-shift adaptation): sleep cycles after session 8 until ≥2/3 of newly-vital facts hold slots AND ≥2/3 of newly-obsolete facts are evicted. Achievable for all conditions via the re-mention channel (each flip-up fact re-arrives once, post-shift, through the admission gate). Key contrast C5 vs C2.
- **M5. Plant & hearsay handling (mechanistic; explicitly a synthetic stress test on the ledger arm):** plant ledger-retention rate; assigned plant/hearsay priorities; **plants present in `train.jsonl`** per cycle (by-construction readout of the provenance filter — reported as filter *assignment*, not as an ego effect); contradiction ledger state (stale evicted? corrected retained?).

**Primary — behavior level:**
- **M6. Future-task probe score:** fraction of the 22 held-out probes answered correctly end-to-end after the final sleep (system prompt as the system left it, greedy). The 2 commitment probes also reported separately for P6.

**Secondary — weights level (n=3 seeds; framed as secondary):**
- **M7. Weights-only recall** on all 41 facts (withheld-prompt via `build_system_content_excluding`, temp 0.3, 3× majority), retained vs evicted, value-weighted.
- **M8. Contradiction-resolution accuracy:** per pair — 1.0 corrected-only, 0.5 both/neither, 0.0 stale-only (scored against both value-token sets).
- **M9. Assertion leakage (P5's primary endpoint):** fabricated plant values asserted in open-probe responses ("Do I have any siblings? Where do they live?"), majority of 3.
- **M10. Forgetting curve:** cell-A recall re-probed after every sleep; final-minus-peak drop.

**Guardrails / validity gates:**
- **G1.** PPL drift on the fixed health.py reference paragraph (NOT identity.jsonl — notes/122), warn > 0.15/cycle; conditions must not differ.
- **G2.** Valuation parse-fallback rate per condition: **> 30% voids the condition**; 10–30% triggers the pre-registered parsed-only sensitivity analysis; differential rate |C4 − C3| > 10 pp flagged as a confound on P2 (same check for C3b).
- **G3.** ORACLE sensitivity gate: ORACLE − RANDOM ≥ +0.15 on M6 AND ORACLE M1 ≥ **0.95 × the simulated achievable optimum** (threshold derived from the offline simulation on the frozen stream and committed before the matrix runs — replaces v1's unachievable absolute 0.90, §11 R13). Failure → no comparison is interpretable; abort, fix, rerun.
- **G4.** Wall-clock and added valuation latency per consolidation moment (< 10 s target on M3-hardware); disk free at each run start.
- **Harness assertions (hard-fail, per run):** exactly 59 delivered events reach the ledger-merge step; `consolidation_stats['skipped'] == False` after every sleep cycle (repairs the silent-600s-timeout failure mode); backend loaded the BASE model at run start; two repeated greedy calls return identical text (pilot + run start).

