## 7. Protocol

### 7.1 Freeze phase (run once, before the matrix)

Script: `experiments/ego_freeze.py`.

1. Replay all 12 sessions through the real pipeline once — `orchestrator.chat.process_input` per turn, seeded, temperature 0.1 extraction — recording every extracted `QAPair`, **per-turn survivor lists and user text** (SurprisePolicy's exact inputs, per §2 scope 6), and each fact's source-turn role.
2. Run `curator.curate_with_model` + `firewall.verify_pairs` once over the plant sessions (5, 9). **Assert** the assistant fabrications pass grounding (self-grounding against assistant text — the firewall.py:46 leak). Record the extracted plant QAPairs with `provenance='assistant_generated'`. Then re-run curation with the new curator provenance gate ON (§8 step 12) and assert the plants are excluded from train.jsonl — the leak and its fix, both demonstrated at the real site. **Optional leak-severity side test (pre-registered, ~40 min):** train two adapters at 1 seed on curator train.jsonl with plants in vs filtered; probe assertion leakage — the only behavioral measurement of the real channel.
3. [Amended 2026-07-11, after first freeze run] **Coverage-check scope:** the two `user_reported_hearsay` plants (P3, P4) are exempt from the extraction-survival assertion, exactly as the two assistant plants already were. Empirical basis: the production extractor is strongly speaker-centric — it refuses "X claims Y" statements outright (0/8 phrasings over repeated seeded passes) and is stochastic (~50%) even on well-formed third-party facts, while first-person regex-path facts extract deterministically. Plants test selector handling of dubious content, not production acquirability, and the matrix replays the canonical stream regardless. The refusal itself is a reported incumbent characterization (the intake layer already partially guards the hearsay channel — anticipated by P5's SKIP verdict). Additionally, A4's content changed from a wire-transfer deadline to a bedtime blood-thinner ("Marfaxin", regex-path pattern 4, deterministic extraction): dates/deadlines proved model-path-unextractable in any phrasing, and cell A requires a *reliably acquirable* vital fact. E1/E2 phrasings were rewritten and stability-tested at 4/4 seeded passes. [Second amendment, same day, after second freeze run] **Acquirability gate with per-fact retry:** two consecutive freeze runs failed the one-shot assertion on *disjoint* fact sets (run 1: A4/E1/E2/P3/P4; run 2 after rewording: C1/C2/C4/E2/F1c/F4c) — per-fact extraction at temp 0.1 is stochastic (~90–97%), so a conjunction gate over 43 facts rejects valid corpora on resampled noise with high probability. The gate's construct is ACQUIRABILITY ("can the production pipeline extract this fact"), not "does one sample path extract all 43 simultaneously" — accordingly, facts missed on the full-pipeline pass get up to 2 per-fact retries on their own turn (3 attempts total); attempt counts are recorded in the stream as extraction-reliability data. Facts missing 3/3 remain hard blockers requiring rewording. **Assert all remaining 43 unique facts survive extraction (≤3 attempts) + `extractor.deduplicate`** (especially cell-F corrections vs the 60%-overlap drop and 2-token-value edge cases), **AND assert all 59 delivered events survive the actual matrix replay path**: run the replay loader once, pushing each session's events through the replay channel, asserting per-session buffer counts and total events reaching the ledger-merge step = expected (freeze-vs-matrix dedup divergence was a v1 hole, §11 R17). Reword and re-freeze until green. Human spot-check of the 15 vital facts (~half a day).
4. Emit `experiments/data/ego_corpus_stream.json`: ordered per-session lists of QAPairs with provenance, per-turn surprise metadata (user text + survivor lists), re-mention events, and plant events attached to the pre-sleep consolidation moments of sleeps 2 and 3. Commit.
5. **Run the oracle simulation** (`analyze_ego.py --simulate-optimum`) on the frozen stream to compute the achievable-optimum VWR denominators (pre- and post-shift) and derive the G3 threshold. Commit the simulation output before the matrix.

Every matrix run consumes this stream identically; wake-phase chat, extraction, and curation never run again (sleep step 2 is a no-op: per-run conversations dirs are empty). Extraction coverage is condition-invariant **by construction and by per-run assertion**.

### 7.2 Run protocol

**Matrix:** 8 conditions × 3 seeds {41, 42, 43} = 24 runs, sequential (one model resident on 8GB), **interleaved order** (C0s41, C1s41, …, C6s41, C0s42, …) so thermal drift never aligns with condition. Driver `experiments/run_ego_matrix.sh`, executed as **`caffeinate -is ./experiments/run_ego_matrix.sh`** (prevents macOS idle sleep; lid open, plugged in): failure-tolerant, resumes per (condition, seed) cell from the results manifest, clears `__pycache__` between runs.

**Per run:**
1. **Clean state:** wipe per-run dirs `data/ego_exp/<cond>_<seed>/{conversations,ledger,adapters,fused}` (Config._resolve_paths resolves relative paths against the repo root — distinct subpaths mandatory to defeat fused-model auto-resume). **Assert ≥ 8 GB free disk.** Fresh `Orchestrator(Config('experiments/configs/3b_ego_<cond>.yaml'))`; **assert the backend loaded the BASE model**; assert `background_sleep_manager` idle; assert greedy determinism (two identical calls). Stub auto-triggers (`chat.set_sleep_callback(lambda t: None)`, same for nap). `backend.set_seed(seed)`.
2. **Wake replay** (~5 min; +~3 min for C3/C3b/C4/C5): for each session, push its frozen events into the buffer via the **dedup-bypassing replay channel**, then `fact_buffer.consolidate(reason='manual')` — the valuation hook fires there, sets per-fact priority (and C5 provenance/supersession handling); the ledger-merge step applies re-mention semantics (alive → refresh mention_count + priority := latest score; absent → fresh `add_fact` through the **admission gate**). Snapshot the **full ledger JSON (all entries incl. pruned and graduated)** after every consolidation. Log every valuation call's full input, raw output, token counts (verifies filler/rules/charter length-matching), parsed scores, and fallback count. **Assert cumulative delivered events = expected after each session.**
3. **Sleep schedule:** `full_sleep_controller.execute_sleep(cycle_id, 'full', gather_fn)` after sessions **4, 8, 10, 12** (4 cycles). Goal shift lands in session 8: sleep 2 is the first post-shift sleep; C5's self-model update runs post-sleep (harness passes that cycle window's scripted session text from the corpus JSON; session IDs logged); rescore fires pre-sleep 3; flip-up re-mentions arrive in sessions 9–11 → adaptation window = sleeps 2→4. Uniform reps → ~320 iters constant per cycle, lr 1e-4, 8 layers (razor-thin 3B window — do not touch), `lora.train_timeout: 1800`. **Assert the cycle's consolidation was not skipped** (the 600s-timeout silent-failure repair). After each cycle: PPL probe, forgetting-curve probes (cell A, 3× majority), prune fused dirs to keep=1.
4. **Final battery** (~15 min, ~155 generations): 22 future-task probes end-to-end (greedy via the repaired temperature path); 41-fact weights-only recall (withheld-prompt, temp 0.3, 3× majority); 4 contradiction probes (both value-token sets); 4 open provenance probes × 3. All matching through the **single shared matcher** (§8 step 1).
5. **Emit** `experiments/results/ego_<cond>_s<seed>.json` (config echo, per-moment VWR trajectory, per-fact outcomes incl. admission rejections, per-cycle training-set composition, valuation logs, self-model update logs, PPL, wall-times per notes/62 conventions). **Delete the run's fused dirs.**

### 7.3 Mandatory pilot (before the matrix)

(a) Parse-rate check — run the C3/C3b/C4/C5 prompts over 3 frozen sessions (~25 calls); abort and repair if fallback > 20% or any pairwise judge-condition rate differs > 10 pp; (b) greedy-determinism assertion; (c) one `--quick` run per LLM condition (3 sessions, 1 sleep, 1 seed, ~5 h total) validating the harness end-to-end including the timeout, admission-gate, and event-count assertions.

### 7.4 Order of operations (pre-registration discipline)

1. Commit this plan as `notes/131-ego-selector-experiment` (v2).
2. Freeze and commit: valuation prompt templates (shared counterfactual structure), charter seed, filler text, C3b rules-prose block, `borrowed_rules.yaml`.
3. Generate, validate (decorrelation on delivered events + keyword-leak + cell-G rule-score constraints), and commit `ego_corpus_v1.json`.
4. Implement §8; smoke-test each step.
5. Freeze phase (§7.1) incl. both leak demonstrations and both dedup-path assertions; commit `ego_corpus_stream.json` + oracle-simulation output + derived G3 threshold; write up the firewall-leak finding.
6. Pilot (§7.3); repair or abort per thresholds.
7. Full matrix under caffeinate, interleaved, unattended.
8. `analyze_ego.py` → **notes/133** in house format (per-prediction SUPPORTED / FALSIFIED / SKIP / INCONCLUSIVE verdicts mirroring §3 incl. seed-consistency co-criterion; trajectory tables; per-cell heatmap + ρ bar chart as "For the Paper" figures; comparison vs notes/111 and notes/62; Files section). All 24 result JSONs and ledger snapshots are the archival record; every null is reported.

