## 10. Runtime and disk budget

**Per run:** wake replay ~5 min (C3/C3b/C4/C5: +~3 min for 12–14 greedy scoring calls) + 4 sleep cycles × ~11–15 min (≈320 LoRA iters 6–9 min + fuse subprocess 2–3 min + ≤8 graduation generations + PPL + forgetting probes; paraphrase augmentation pinned to 0) + final battery **~15 min** (~155 generations at ~5–7 s) ≈ **65–95 min/run**.
**Matrix:** 24 runs ≈ **26–38 h**, unattended across two nights + a day under caffeinate, plugged in, resumable per cell. One-time costs: corpus authoring + freeze + human verification ≈ 1 day; implementation ≈ 2–3 days; pilot ≈ 5 h.
**Disk:** fused dirs pruned to keep=1 during a run and deleted at run end → peak ~4 GB transient against ~18 GiB free; free space asserted at every run start.
**Pre-registered trim ladder if behind schedule:** (1) ORACLE and RANDOM drop to 2 seeds (−2 runs; they anchor floor/ceiling, not headline contrasts); (2) JUDGE-RULES drops to 2 seeds (−1 run; P2b then requires 2/2 sign consistency); (3) forgetting-curve probes only after sleeps 2 and 4; (4) — least preferred — drop the sleep after session 10 (shrinks the revaluation window to 2 cycles).

